  "text": "Recipe: Oven Roasted Fries\nCreator: Kiran Sharma\nCategory: Fries\nIngredients: 4 russet potatoes, paprika, 21 Seasoning Salute Blend, black pepper powder, dried parsley\nCooking methods: bake, boil, no-cook\nInstructions: PREP: (a) Preheat the oven to 420F. (b) Scrub the potatoes clean. I left the peel on.\nCook the potatoes partially. I cooked them in a pressure cooker (opened 5 minutes after the first whistle). At this point, potatoes were half cooked.\nChop the half cooked potatoes into fries of any shape; wedges with thickness 1/2\" to 3/4\" are recommended.\nToss potato wedges into a large bowl. Sprinkle some water and any seasonings of your choice. Mix well.\nPlace the seasoned wedges inside a baking tray lined with a Silicone Mat, making sure they do not touch.\nBake for 35-40 minutes. Turn them over after 20 minutes. Cook them until they turn golden brown and crispy.\nServe with Garlic Tahini!\nNOTE: Sprinkling some water on potato wedges, helps the seasoning to adhere and avoid burning.\nNotes: Sprinkling some water on potato wedges, helps the seasoning to adhere and avoid burning.",
